WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:11.160
71. Desertification. Some people say desertification is the biggest

2
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.520
environmental problem for our planet. What is desertification? Why does it

3
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.880
happen? How can we stop it? Desertification is what happens when dry

4
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:28.560
areas become very damaged. These areas can be very delicate. Natural events or

5
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.440
human activities can change the important balance of water in dry land

6
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.680
areas. When the plants dry up and the ways to hold water in an area are gone,

7
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.920
the land becomes what we would call a desert. Desertification is bad for

8
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.440
agriculture and biodiversity. Desertification has always happened in

9
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:56.600
the world. Natural events like long droughts can cause desertification. But

10
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.920
now human activity causes most desertification. Slash and burn

11
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.160
agriculture, in which trees are cut and burned to clear land for farming, can

12
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:14.180
lead to desertification as roots stop soil from eroding. Overgrazing, when

13
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.760
animals eat too much grass in an area, can also cause it. Planting non-native

14
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.760
plants in dry areas can change the balance of the ecosystem and lead to

15
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:30.400
desertification. Then there is more poverty, less food, and more hunger for

16
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:37.760
people in the area. So, how can we stop desertification? Most importantly, we need

17
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:43.640
to prevent it from starting. It is easier to protect dry lands than to restore

18
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.360
them. Preventing soil from eroding is very important for preventing

19
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:53.520
desertification. Simple things like putting stones around tree trunks can

20
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.040
help because the stones collect dew for the tree's roots. Living trees are

21
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.840
important for holding on to soil. Even after lands have been degraded, they can

22
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:11.960
still be helped. Reforestation, planting new forests, is one solution. Desertification

23
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:17.560
is happening fast and affecting many people. We must learn how desertification

24
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:24.280
happens and how to prevent it, or we will face more pain and poverty.
